                <p class="snippet" >
                    Representation by spouses, relatives, in-laws or friends is only allowed in cases falling within the <b>jurisdiction</b> of the <b>small claims</b> division of the Court of Québec (art. 959 C.C.P.). &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;. . . In the case of proceedings in the <b>small claims</b> court under Book VIII of the Code of Civil Procedure, however, art. 959 allows physical persons to “give a mandate to their spouse, a relative, a person connected by marriage or a friend to represent them”. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;As I noted earlier, representation by spouses, relatives, in-laws or friends is only allowed in cases falling within the <b>jurisdiction</b> of the <b>small claims</b> division of the Court of Québec pursuant to art. 959 C.C.P. 
