                <p class="snippet" >
                    In that case, the <b>jurisdiction</b> was broadly defined as <b>jurisdiction</b> over lessor-lessee relations. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;Wilson J. referred to “<b>jurisdiction</b> in 1867" or “1867 <b>jurisdiction</b>”, but nowhere stipulated for one particular moment in time. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;85 In the case at bar, where <b>jurisdiction</b> over residential tenancy disputes is in question, the evidence clearly shows that <b>small claims</b> for rent could be heard by the Justices of the Peace throughout Nova Scotia in exercising their <b>jurisdiction</b> in debt. 
