</li>
    <li class="even list-item-expanded">
<div class="number">
    <span class="digits">20.</span>
</div>
<div class="metadata">
    <div class="info" >
        <div class="subinfo">
            <h3>
                <span class="title"><a target="_parent" href="/scc-csc/scc-csc/en/item/413/index.do?q=%22Small+Claims%22+jurisdiction">Sobeys Stores Ltd. v. Yeomans and Labour Standards Tribunal (N.S.)</a></span>
                    - <span class="report-citation">[1989] 1 SCR 238</span>
                - <span class="publicationDate">1989-03-02</span>
            </h3>
            <div class="subMetadata">
                <span>Supreme Court Judgments</span>
            </div> 
            <div class="subject">
                    <span>
                            Constitutional law<br/>
                    </span>
            </div> 
                <p class="snippet" >
                    Pre-Confederation <b>jurisdiction</b> refers to pre-1867 <b>jurisdiction</b> and not to <b>jurisdiction</b> in a particular province immediately prior to that province's joining confederation. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;The test of 1867 <b>jurisdiction</b> must include an examination of the <b>jurisdiction</b> in all four original confederating provinces, and if this results in a tie, the <b>jurisdiction</b> in the United Kingdom. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Jurisdiction</b> in debt, however, is not to be equated to <b>jurisdiction</b> over unjust dismissal. 
                </p>
